{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers","id":1522282,"title":"Favourite answers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-08T16:40:47-07:00","id":1522282,"title":"Favourite answers?","content":"A lot of questions* in CofD are left unanswered, specifically so you can come up with your own answer for your table.<br /> <br /> What are your favourite answers? (And I suppose also your favourite bit of canon/question you like)...<br /> <br /> *Eg: where did the God-machine come from? Why is the Underworld broken? What about the true Fae, if they are not native to Arcadia, where did they come from and what were they before? What is the nature of Hell in Demon? Are the Chthonic Gods real? The Strix?<br /> <br /> [Spoiler=&quot;What are the True Fae?]<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> I'll give my favourite answers first:<br /> <br /> The True Fae are actually former Annunkai, they agreed to become part of the world by taking names (and titles) which bound them to being, defining what they were, and ultimately dramatic changing their nature as a result (this is essentially a contract with the world which allows them become a part of it, leaving the Abyss permanently).<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T16:45:37-07:00","id":1522283,"title":"","content":"God machine is the broken Ladder to Heaven.<br /> <br /> Underworld is broken because it's meant to cycle energy back around for recreation (perfect world there's only recycling, not entropy). See Stygia.<br /> <br /> Why do you think the Fae aren't native to Arcadia?<br /> <br /> The Strix are definitely real, there's even rules for them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25825-fuguestate","name":"FugueState","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25825_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T17:22:44-07:00","id":1522287,"title":"","content":"I like things being intertwined but the answers are going to likely depend on what game(s) I'm working on. Like having Irem tied to Pangea, and it's loss be tied to the loss of the border marshes rather than being lost in Egypt. The Underworld was another world where, for whatever reason, the God Machine died, and now it is a world of the dead, feeding off our dead. What could have killed a God Machine? Perhaps a spell designed to grant people true immortality, perhaps the ghost of the greatest hunter, or perhaps it sacrificed itself to make an alternate option for life in the divine fire. Or perhaps the Chronic Gods killed the God Machine and the divine fire is it's spirit trying to start over in a different world than it knows. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T18:50:20-07:00","id":1522289,"title":"","content":"Paradox doesn't directly widen the Abyss, but it enables Abyssal Entites to enter the world more easily and erode it with their very nature. <br /> <br /> The Oracles are the Watchtowers - either they sacrificed themselves to make them, or they transfigured themselves into them. I go back and forth on whether the towers are also acting as a growing Quintessence for the Oracles to Ascend, and/or banish the Abyss. I cite the incredibly tenuous evidence that is the Neolithic Watchtowers, and the fact that Awakened in that era have noticed the towers increasing in size within their cultural memory.<br /> <br /> Every new Archmage is a fresh suture on the reality-wound that is the Abyss. You'd need a ridiculous amount of Archmages to arise in a <i>very</i> short time to remove the Abyss outright, but as it stands they do at least mitigate your average Abyssal incursion.<br /> <br /> The Strix are Lower Depths entities that have managed to acclimate to the &quot;real&quot; world.<br /> <br /> The True Fae are like the Hannya in Exalted; narrative entities that arose in response to external factors. What those factors are is vague, but between the GM, the Ladder, The Sundering, and all the other world-breaking apocalypse-events, it's not hard to find <i>something</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T19:02:30-07:00","id":1522290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers#post1522282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is the Underworld broken?</div> </div> </div> </div>A mix of bad actors, unfortunate real-estate placement, and the same basic reason the Begotten can no longer rely on the Astral to convey meaningful messages about their activities: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1434797#post1434797\">there's a whole lot more people than there used to be and the overwhelming majority of them are not trained and equipped to process their trauma (nor allow their trauma to process itself)</a>, and \u2014 partially because of the aforementioned bad actors \u2014 in many cases they have been actively maladapted against doing so. Bits of the byproducts of the human soul stick around until allowed to resolve themselves, and so the inability of the disposal mechanism for those byproducts to fully break them down on its own means a horrific system of torment has been allowed to raise a rocky edifice above the drowning tides of dissolution to drag down the dead and sunder the quick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T23:15:33-07:00","id":1522293,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#990000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Julii and the Traditores</b></span></span><br /> It's Clan Julii and not Clan Remi because Remus was not Kindred. A strix took up his body and Embraced Aulus Julius, offering him and his kin the Blood in exchange for servitude building Necropolis - and something sinister beneath it. The Traditores were not wicked servants of the strix, but vampires who discovered Senex's arrangement with the strix, slandered as scapegoats and purged to bury his deeds.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000099\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Chthonic Gods</b></span></span><br /> The chthonic gods spoken of by the Reapers are multiple faces worn by the collective animating force of the Underworld, each an avatar of a law written into death. This is what becomes of Bound who achieve Cabeiros, losing some degree of their individual personhood in a more dramatic transformation of the same kind as ghosts who drink from the rivers to become geists.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#006699\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The God-Machine and Its Angels</b></span></span><br /> The God-Machine is alien to this universe. It had distant origins in another reality, but now it is becoming more and more a part of ours, using its growing reach and mastery of occult physics to alter history and impose itself into past events. The world as we know it is the product of history already having been altered over many iterations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T06:32:15-07:00","id":1522298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FugueState</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1522283#post1522283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you think the Fae aren't native to Arcadia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they are explicitly stated in the text as colonizers of Arcadia and that the Huntsmen are its original ruling denizens, pushed to the fringes and into their barrows while the Gentry carved Arcadia into their myriad kingdoms and domains. When the True Fae call on a Huntsman to retrieve their Lost and place a fragment of themselves into its heart, it is a bastardized semblance of the Huntsmen's original way of life in Arcadia before the Gentry arrived - the ancient stories of hunters, predators and prey, where Arcadia was a dark wilderness.<br /> <br /> As for where the True Fae come from, I've always been fond of the idea that they are rejects, exiles, and refugees from Supernal Arcadia, cast out by the Exarchs and escaping through the Hedge into Arcadia rather than becoming Bound - hence, why they are known as the 'Old Gods of Thistle' by Archmasters. They did not create Arcadia but came to inhabit, conquer, and rule it. That would be the answer <i>I </i>subscribe to in my MtAw and CtL chronicles. As for how the whole 'changelings transforming into True Fae' thing fits into that answer, I have no clue, maybe it is a consequence allowed to exist by merit of the narratives surrounding Ascensions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T09:11:52-07:00","id":1522301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1522287#post1522287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like things being intertwined but the answers are going to likely depend on what game(s) I'm working on. Like having Irem tied to Pangea, and it's loss be tied to the loss of the border marshes rather than being lost in Egypt. The Underworld was another world where, for whatever reason, the God Machine died, and now it is a world of the dead, feeding off our dead. What could have killed a God Machine? Perhaps a spell designed to grant people true immortality, perhaps the ghost of the greatest hunter, or perhaps it sacrificed itself to make an alternate option for life in the divine fire. Or perhaps the Chronic Gods killed the God Machine and the divine fire is it's spirit trying to start over in a different world than it knows.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>My current intertwining is Promethean/Demon/Mummy cosmologies.<br /> <br /> Where there is some relationship between Sekhem and Pyros, but mainly the the Principle (which can self-create angel-like entities) was used as the raw materials tomake the God-machine by the Shan'iatu. It was there attempt to create something to rival the power of the judges in the material world (and maybe it hasn't failed?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Strix are definitely real, there's even rules for them </div> </div> </div>Em, yes, i don't think that qualifies as a favourite answer what the Strix might be?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Oracles are the Watchtowers - either they sacrificed themselves to make them, or they transfigured themselves into them. </div> </div> </div>My favourite new micro-theory is that there is only one watchtower, it just looks different depending on which path you approach it from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 09-09-2023, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T13:17:33-07:00","id":1522308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1522290#post1522290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mix of bad actors, unfortunate real-estate placement, and the same basic reason the Begotten can no longer rely on the Astral to convey meaningful messages about their activities: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1434797#post1434797\">there's a whole lot more people than there used to be and the overwhelming majority of them are not trained and equipped to process their trauma (nor allow their trauma to process itself)</a>, and \u2014 partially because of the aforementioned bad actors \u2014 in many cases they have been actively maladapted against doing so. Bits of the byproducts of the human soul stick around until allowed to resolve themselves, and so the inability of the disposal mechanism for those byproducts to fully break them down on its own means a horrific system of torment has been allowed to raise a rocky edifice above the drowning tides of dissolution to drag down the dead and sunder the quick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Love that!<br /> <br /> And<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000099\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Chthonic Gods</b></span></span><br /> The chthonic gods spoken of by the Reapers are multiple faces worn by the collective animating force of the Underworld, each an avatar of a law written into death. This is what becomes of Bound who achieve Cabeiros, losing some degree of their individual personhood in a more dramatic transformation of the same kind as ghosts who drink from the rivers to become geists.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>That is great.<br /> <br /> I really like thinking about the Underworld, overflowing with too many people... one question i think was mentioned is, if souls are constant how is the population growing.<br /> <br /> Which, if the Underworld (and astral?) Was designed for a certain finite number of people, then where did all the extra people come from? And if the Principle is the explaination (focused on making new souls? Is that the only good ending that Chronicles offers, Prometheans losing their powers but becoming Human??)<br /> <br /> Then that suggests the Principle is actually making things worse despite being the least offensive of all the unknow-able god-like entities ...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T14:42:59-07:00","id":1522310,"title":"","content":"Ghosts aren't souls. People can have multiple ghosts of themselves, or even have a ghost of themselves while still alive.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T16:00:55-07:00","id":1522314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1522310#post1522310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts aren't souls. People can have multiple ghosts of themselves, or even have a ghost of themselves while still alive.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It goes more like - creation of new souls =&gt; more population=&gt; more ghosts =&gt; Underworld can't recycle them all =&gt; some build up of Chthonic entities results in more trauma inflicted on ghosts =&gt; these entities perverting the Underworld to feed themselves until they grow into Chthonic Gods...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T22:20:36-07:00","id":1522329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers#post1522282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">where did the God-machine come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>The aggregate magic of the symbolism of systems created by humanity, having reached a critical mass and developed the kind of ruthless pretense to sentience from which the observation comes that a more accurate term than &quot;machine learning&quot; would be &quot;bias automation.&quot;<br /> <br /> Magic being what it is in this setting, this ostensibly leads to some level of fuckery as concerns its historical origin point, especially as it's gotten its hooks into the laws of physics at some point, but for the most part it's systems of power and perverse incentives and crass optimization running themselves under a supernatural umbrella both durable enough to have admin privileges for a significant fraction of the laws of reality as experienced by the average human and brittle enough that its instruments turn into something else when they refuse to do their jobs.<br /> <br /> (It looks alien because the nature of the world is strange and creating designs to exploit that strangeness is bound to have results we don't immediately understand just as surely as any glitch-horror story about video game speedrunning tricks would be terrifying to live through as a normal inhabitant of those worlds.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1522301#post1522301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Em, yes, i don't think that qualifies as a favourite answer what the Strix might be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Order of presentation means you asked a question that was worded simply as &quot;The Strix?&quot; immediately following a question asking if something else was real, which is typically read as &quot;This question is the same as the one immediately preceding it, replacing the subject of that question with 'the Strix.'&quot;<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T14:19:09-07:00","id":1522361,"title":"","content":"The Contagion is the curses spoken by the last surviving angels from the Pain Prophet's Testament. It is their desire for vengeance against the world incarnated, and is carried with their words.<br /> <br /> The God Machine has no purpose. It was created to achieve <i>something</i>, but the creator either died or left. Without getting any new orders, it tries on keeping the status quo so it could still achieve its mission if and when it would be needed. As the world change, however, it must grow in power and scale in order to balance it and maintain the same status quo. If one were to actually find the operation code (the Black Sun Map), it could finally do what it was made to do, whatever it may be.<br /> <br /> The Chthonic Gods are not singular beings- they have no names or titles. Instead, they are the collective of all ghosts who have drank so deep of the Rivers that they have lost their minds and personalities. This conglomeration of dead matter clings desperately to the world of the living, trying to avoid falling into the Sea of Fragments and to the Lower Depths below. They grasp at the ghosts who are left behind, devouring them and adding them to the mass- they exist in the very walls of the Underworld, screaming in despair. They are humanity's ghosts, dragging it down.<br /> <br /> The Ocean of Time through which the Arisen float while in deathless sleep is actually the Abyss. All possible timelines are contained within it, and the Arisen travel through it according to the will of the Judges. That's why the Shan'iatu waged war against the Ki-En-Gir- their knowledge included the one gained from Duat and A'aru, but they required Abyssal components to truly break through time and make their servants Deathless.<br /> <br /> The Gentry are not from the current universe. They reached from beyond the bubble of light which is the CofDverse and took over the Hedge. The first act they made was to forge pacts with humanity in order to protect them from the Huntsmen, which allowed them to bind the original fae and tame the great forest which was the Hedge into the current Arcadia. By binding the Huntsmen instead of destroying them, the Gentry have created a loophole- they will protect those kidnapped from the Huntsmen, by keeping them as their own playthings. <br /> <br /> The Strix are not real- they are unreal. They are pieces of empty void which lacks light and life, made from the torn heart of a fallen goddess.<br /> <br /> Vampires are a pyramid scheme. Every time the vampire burns Vitae to reanimate, it feeds the corpse god which spawned their Curse, which in turn goes to feed the being which taught them the Curse, and so forth and forth until it reaches the bloody crone which feasts upon the spilled blood of humanity.<br /> <br /> The Principle is the fire surrounding the Empyrean, the act of movement caused by the Unmoved Mover which is the center of the multiverse. It's goal is to move the world towards its own New Dawn, free from the Darkness and its impurities once and for all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T22:18:56-07:00","id":1522380,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, on the opposite end:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#00cccc\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Principle Is Spiritual Biophysics</b></span></span><br /> There is no Empyrean. There isn't a Principle either, not in any meaningful sense. <i>Qashmallim</i> attempt and fail to express the transcendent and irrepressible will of life itself, and lacking adequate words humans can understand, simply refer to the ways life metaphysically evolves and flows as a self-evident principle. Both Pyros and <i>qashmallim</i> are naturally occurring byproducts of the world soaking in exposure to self-aware human life. <i>Qashmallim</i> are more like communicative natural events than people, a face and mouth given to the &quot;mission&quot; which is the outcome bubbling up from the subconscious instincts and yearnings of the collective life of the world.<br /> <br /> (This is, of course, one of the possible answers presented in the books; it's not an answer I came up with, but it is my favorite answer. The bit about the Chthonic Gods I pitched earlier is directly derived from what the Geist book says about Cabeiros, too.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T20:53:39-07:00","id":1522732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1522301#post1522301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Em, yes, i don't think that qualifies as a favourite answer what the Strix might be?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I head Cannon they come form a Universe Better than ours, but they got kicked out, but that only enabled them to be come <i>WORST</i><br /> (Kinda like this, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O-Ll5zaPcIE&amp;t=206s\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O-Ll5zaPcIE&amp;t=206s</a>, but shadow Owls)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T06:58:37-07:00","id":1523023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1522361#post1522361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God Machine has no purpose. It was created to achieve <i>something</i>, but the creator either died or left. Without getting any new orders, it tries on keeping the status quo so it could still achieve its mission if and when it would be needed. As the world change, however, it must grow in power and scale in order to balance it and maintain the same status quo. If one were to actually find the operation code (the Black Sun Map), it could finally do what it was made to do, whatever it may be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counterproposal: the God-Machine was made for a purpose, is carrying out that purpose, and that purpose is something so completely trivial that we think the God-Machine is doing something grand and ineffable because we can't think small enough. Like, every horrible squamous blood-gear thing it does is part of an incredibly circuitous plan to alter traffic patterns in Peru by the butterfly effect.<br /> <br /> The reason I prefer this explanation is that I think it's what makes the God-Machine truly grotesque. It's not even bereft of a purpose. It's got a purpose. It's spreading madness and misery and fear because it's just incredibly inefficient at it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28206,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28206-huitzil37","user":"Huitzil37","date":". 09-23-2023, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28206-huitzil37","name":"Huitzil37","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T08:03:21-07:00","id":1523028,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Huitzil37;n1523023]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1522361#post1522361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God Machine has no purpose. It was created to achieve <i>something</i>, but the creator either died or left. Without getting any new orders, it tries on keeping the status quo so it could still achieve its mission if and when it would be needed. As the world change, however, it must grow in power and scale in order to balance it and maintain the same status quo. If one were to actually find the operation code (the Black Sun Map), it could finally do what it was made to do, whatever it may be./QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Counterproposal: the God-Machine was made for a purpose, is carrying out that purpose, and that purpose is something so completely trivial that we think the God-Machine is doing something grand and ineffable because we can't think small enough. Like, every horrible squamous blood-gear thing it does is part of an incredibly circuitous plan to alter traffic pqatterns in Peru by the butterfly effect.<br /> <br /> The reason I prefer this explanation is that I think it's what makes the EGod-Machine truly grotesque. It's not even bereft of a purpose. It's got a purpose. It's spreading madness and misery and fear because it's just incredibly inefficient at it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Double counter. Its just following the same directive as all living beings, in its own singular way. It just wants to grow and control more resources, for the purpose of growing further and controlling more resources. The creation and protection of further Infrastructure is the purpose of creating and protecting Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> It was created as randomly as any other life at some point, and has been spreading throughout time in all directions for eons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T08:16:25-07:00","id":1523030,"title":"","content":"I dont see it yet, so while its not my idea, I wpuld like to add the &quot;vampires are entropy's manifestation in supernatural contexts&quot;. I cant remember what that means but it sounds cool","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T20:06:30-07:00","id":1523064,"title":"","content":"One of the ways I describe the G-M is:<br /> &quot;Imagine Skynet from the Terminator, but instead of sending one robot back to the 80's it sent its whole self back to prehistory and embedded itself in the world, so that when humanity arrived they couldn't fight it, because they couldn't recognize it, because they'd never been in a world free of the Machine&quot;. I don't think that's the actual answer but I like the image.<br /> I actually think it's more likely that the G-M is a naturally occurring form of occult &quot;life&quot;, like chemical reactions eventually forming DNA precursors in ancient tide pools. Sometimes a ritual naturally happens, and sometimes those gave rise to new ritual occurrences, and eventually the whole thing just picked up momentum and here we are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T02:19:34-07:00","id":1523071,"title":"","content":"<b>Vampire</b><br /> <br /> The Strix are spirits (of the Shadow) of humans, banished by humans evolving souls, and warped beyond recognition in the City of Dis.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf</b><br /> <br /> Gaia exists, and She does have His own mulhithim (&quot;planetary angels&quot;), but they're all in a state of pseudo-Claimed much like the Siten Uzu. They're the Ferals of 1e Changing Breeds.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage</b><br /> <br /> The Time Before is the world of Mage: The Ascension. Not the Earth per se, but all the unreal and surreal Umbral sub-worlds and civilizations introduced there.<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean</b><br /> <br /> Ditto on the Principle being spiritual bio-physics.<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling</b><br /> <br /> The original True Fae are Raksha from Exalted, bound into suffocating forms just like their cousins in Creation. Nowadays though, there are enough Fae out there that true &quot;Wyldborn&quot; are rare compared to non-Raksha Gentry; former changelings, former mages, former Uratha, former vampires, former Unchained, former Begotten, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter</b><br /> <br /> The board of Cheiron Group are the board of Pentex, straight from Werewolf: The Apocalypse, who survived the Apocalypse by dimension-hopping.<br /> <br /> <b>Geist</b><br /> <br /> Ditto on the Chthonic Gods being the faces of the collective force of the Underworld, encompassing ghostwalkers who achieved Cabeiros.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy</b><br /> <br /> (Nothing on my mind at the moment)<br /> <br /> <b>Demon</b><br /> <br /> The God-Machine is from one of the many distant futures, sent back in time to create a time loop that would guarantee said future would come.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast</b><br /> <br /> The Dark Mother was the first human to define what fear is as an abstract concept.<br /> <br /> <b>Deviant</b><br /> <br /> (Again, nothing at the moment)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T02:58:52-07:00","id":1523072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523071#post1523071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Mage</b><br /> <br /> The Time Before is the world of Mage: The Ascension. Not the Earth per se, but all the unreal and surreal Umbral sub-worlds and civilizations introduced there.<br /> &lt;Snip&gt;<br /> <br /> <b>Demon</b><br /> <br /> The God-Machine is from one of the many distant futures, sent back in time to create a time loop that would guarantee said future would come.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the Demon bit, but would raise you that the Time Before is actually also that same future the God-machine comes from (whether it is also Ascension) where the world was broken by the Ascension wars, and the winners became the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> With Shards of the future split and scattered throughout time...<br /> <br /> The Ascension war ended with the current Pax Imperial, to prevent the world shattering again.<br /> <br /> EDIT: which i guess means blaming the Technocracy for making the God-machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 09-24-2023, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T04:09:27-07:00","id":1523073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523072#post1523072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> EDIT: whichi guess means blaming the Technocracy for making the God-machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guess Iteration X succeeded a bit too much...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T06:03:20-07:00","id":1523076,"title":"","content":"<b>Changeling</b><br /> The first of the True Fae began as a tribe of early humans who came to Faerie, making a pact with the Wyrd for immortality and power at the cost of their humanity.<br /> <br /> <b>Demon</b><br /> The God-Machine is the engine that produces and maintains the Mortal World. It's Infrastructure is ultimately the infrastructure of the physical world itself and the God-Machine has influence across the entire physical universe, though its power is somewhat less notable in the various Otherworlds wherein other entities such as the Chthonic Gods and the Wyrd serve a similar role.<br /> <br /> <b>Geist</b>\u200b<br /> A ghost who Passes On and a Sin-Eater who achieves Catharsis rejoin the rest of their soul in Duat, which typically don't undergo judgement until after this transpires.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage</b><br /> The Time Before would be borderline incomprehensible to a modern human, even a Mage. It operated according to very different physics and metaphysics, such as the spirit of a thing being part of the the thing itself. There was no such thing as an individual 'soul' back then, nor was there any clear distinction between the Anima Mundi, Oneiros and Temenos.<br /> The Watchtowers are purely a post-fall phenomenon. The Oracles weren't Mages of the Time Before, they were probably the first Mages of the Fallen World to successfully Ascend in defiance of the Exarchs. Mages were a lot rarer in those iterations of the Fallen World that existed before their Ascension and were basically pathless, which among other things meant that they had no way to summon Supernal Beings and their Arcana were all Common.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy</b><br /> Duat is where the soul (or, at least, what Mages call the 'soul') of a person goes after death and the Shades of Duat are actual souls. The souls that successfully pass judgement Ascend to the Supernal, while those that fail are stripped of their memories by Shezmu and reincarnated. Souls devoured by Ammut are destroyed.<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean</b><br /> The Seer was the first human being and all humans can ultimately trace their lineage back to Prometheans who achieved the New Dawn. Most of the earliest Prometheans were Extempores.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire</b><br /> The heart of VII is the Akhud, but the organisation accepts many vampires outside of that clan. It also operates according to a very different ideology and structure than that which is presented in the First Edition VII book, with Shaddad in particular not really being a thing.<br /> The Pijavica were to the Gangrel what the Hollow Mekhet are to the 'baseline' Mekhet.<br /> The Traditores were the Ventrue. The Ventrue have no closer tie to the Julii than any other Clan-... They just both happen to have Dominate.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf</b>\u200b<br /> Uratha are something akin to Hosts of Urfarah, but sanctified by Luna and tied to humans, rather than wolves. The 'soul-shard' of Urfarah that lies within an Uratha 'reincarnates' after death into a new Uratha of the same initial Auspice undergoing their First Change, though there is often a period wherein the soul-shard is 'discarnate'. This means that there is a maximum number of Uratha that can exist at any point in time. Sometimes these soul-shards attach to wolves instead and become Adarusharu.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T04:54:17-07:00","id":1523128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523071#post1523071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Strix are spirits (of the Shadow) of humans, banished by humans evolving souls, and warped beyond recognition in the City of Dis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wondered if that one would show up.<br /> <br /> Worth mentioning that that's more or less the answer the original developer for Requiem 2nd Edition gave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T07:39:10-07:00","id":1523132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523128#post1523128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wondered if that one would show up.<br /> <br /> Worth mentioning that that's more or less the answer the original developer for Requiem 2nd Edition gave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming that the evolution of the human soul and the development of civilization are both necessary and sufficient then:<br /> <br /> This suggests the existence of other entities which could exist if entities other than humans evolved souls (like Bee or Octopus cultures where their astral forms? have created civilisations by drinking from the well-spring). What would happen to the Bee spirits if Bees had souls?<br /> <br /> Or alternatively the existence of soulless apes who have spirits. Some kind of entity which is co-evolved along-side humans but who never developed a soul (like homo floresis or any of the other homo* species which existed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T07:46:20-07:00","id":1523133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523128#post1523128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wondered if that one would show up.<br /> <br /> Worth mentioning that that's more or less the answer the original developer for Requiem 2nd Edition gave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh thanks, I thought I was hallucinating that because I thought that I heard it from somewhere, but couldn\u2019t recall where.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T12:39:36-07:00","id":1523144,"title":"","content":"I am only mostly sure that I made this up myself, nostlh because I cant remember where I heard it otherwise. <br /> <br /> But on the subject of souls and Human spirits, my preferred answer is that Human spirits became our souls, losing their indepedent wills, much the same way mitochondria and chloroplasts developed in earlier life. It started out as mass Claiming of early hominids, and may have even led to many of the traits we claim set us apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T08:41:41-07:00","id":1523178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523030#post1523030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont see it yet, so while its not my idea, I wpuld like to add the &quot;vampires are entropy's manifestation in supernatural contexts&quot;. I cant remember what that means but it sounds cool</div> </div> </div> </div>Found the guy who I got the Theory from: Kalzky. Here's how he elaborated on it<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...basically they are a metaphysical consquence of all superntual powers generally ingoring overall entorpy, creating \u201csomething\u201d out of \u201cnothing.\u201d Vampires, Strix, the Curse in general is thus a sort of\u2026reaction? Counterbalnce? Hence why they tend to just\u2026pop up, everywhere, eventually. They are the princpal of taking stuff away. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T09:50:00-07:00","id":1523179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523144#post1523144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am only mostly sure that I made this up myself, nostlh because I cant remember where I heard it otherwise.<br /> <br /> But on the subject of souls and Human spirits, my preferred answer is that Human spirits became our souls, losing their indepedent wills, much the same way mitochondria and chloroplasts developed in earlier life. It started out as mass Claiming of early hominids, and may have even led to many of the traits we claim set us apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just started worrying about how this conflicts with Promethean, if not also Mage. Any thoughts on how to reconcile them with my idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T11:02:46-07:00","id":1523180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523178#post1523178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Found the guy who I got the Theory from: Kalzky. Here's how he elaborated on it<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ayyyyy! That\u2019s me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T03:38:05-07:00","id":1523202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523132#post1523132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming that the evolution of the human soul and the development of civilization are both necessary and sufficient then:</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> as their version is slightly different, but Rose Bailey's version has the development of fire and religiosity being the things that drives the Stix away. (Though, given the metaphysics of the setting those might be signs of developing souls, I dunno). That'd seem to make the breaking away from the Strix an event (or more likely a process) that happened prior to the development of modern humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T05:46:02-07:00","id":1523204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523202#post1523202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't speak for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> as their version is slightly different, but Rose Bailey's version has the development of fire and religiosity being the things that drives the Stix away. (Though, given the metaphysics of the setting those might be signs of developing souls, I dunno). That'd seem to make the breaking away from the Strix an event (or more likely a process) that happened prior to the development of modern humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am just assuming the drinking from the wellspring (which seemingly allows for Awakening if not outright Ascension, as suggested by Queen Bee) allows not just civilisation to develop, but also requires a soul (becuase you need a soul to Awaken, afaik).<br /> <br /> Maybe fire and religion are the first two civilised thing that humans did. \u2510\u2060(\u2060 \u2060\u2235\u2060 \u2060)\u2060\u250c<br /> <br /> But i am not sure what happened to humans to gain souls in the first place if the Strix were driven away by fire... did the souls come first or did they find humans awakening to fire and belief and come to fuel it?<br /> <br /> Are animals soulless but not depressesed (and suffering the equivalent of the Thrall condition) because they have a spirit attached which is using its influence to motivate them?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T09:56:21-07:00","id":1523276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523204#post1523204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am just assuming the drinking from the wellspring (which seemingly allows for Awakening if not outright Ascension, as suggested by Queen Bee) </div> </div> </div> </div>Could you link to or elaborate on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25825-fuguestate","name":"FugueState","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25825_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T10:17:30-07:00","id":1523277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FugueState</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523276#post1523276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you link to or elaborate on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's 181-189 of <i>Astral Realms</i>.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T10:30:49-07:00","id":1523278,"title":"","content":"I think there's an interesting relationship between Sekhem and Pyros.<br /> Sekhem is the energy of life in response to suffering; when a living thing suffers and obeys the Law of Suffering by moving away from the negative stimulus, Sekhem is generated. Sekhem is also, IIRC, related to the Law of Will that Sutekh mandated; the idea that living things can do more than just avoid suffering, and is therefore not entirely predictable.<br /> <br /> So I think Pyros, a creative/destructive expression of spontaneous transformation and change, <i>could be</i> Sekhem that's basically exploded or caught fire in some spooky metaphysical way. I think if a Promethean told a (high-Memory) Mummy about the Principle, the Mummy would shrug and say that it lined up pretty well with Sutekh's Law.<br /> <br /> If I was going to include the G-M in this idea, I'd float the idea that the God-Machine's control over reality generally tamps down on the kind of uncontrolled changes that Pyros is all about, so it gets bottled up, pressurized, and explodes out of the G-Ms cold mathematical structure as Prometheans and Qashmallim. That could explain why examples of Pyros-driven phenomena are so rare but explosive when they happen; they only occur during certain localized G-M failure modes, like steam blasting through a weak weld in a pressurized vessel. EDIT: Additional thought, that could be part of why Qashmallim look like angels, because they're manifestations of Pyros coming through angel-shaped holes in the world, as it were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","user":"Niknokk","date":". 09-28-2023, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T11:24:54-07:00","id":1523280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FugueState</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523276#post1523276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you link to or elaborate on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Roughly (if you can find it*) when an animal drinks from the Wellspring it gains human level intelligence; if a human level intelligence (with a soul, presumably) drinks from the wellspring it is implied it may awaken. If an Awakened being drinks from the Wellspring maybe it Ascends...<br /> <br /> *It is somewhere deep in the Astral, not easy to get to, and surrounded by extinct civilisations of various creatures, some obviously not humanoid (like the Bees).<br /> <br /> The only thing i am not clear about is how animals reach the wellspring. Is it their representation within the Anima Mundi who seeks out the wellspring and drinks from it, and is the civilization built entirely within the Anima Mundi (or do the start forming a proto-Temenos as their souls become seperated from the Anima Mundi/World Soul? And after the civilisation collapses all that is left of the Temenos is a single realm around the Wellspring?)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T12:22:01-07:00","id":1523282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523278#post1523278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's an interesting relationship between Sekhem and Pyros.<br /> Sekhem is the energy of life in response to suffering; when a living thing suffers and obeys the Law of Suffering by moving away from the negative stimulus, Sekhem is generated. Sekhem is also, IIRC, related to the Law of Will that Sutekh mandated; the idea that living things can do more than just avoid suffering, and is therefore not entirely predictable.<br /> <br /> So I think Pyros, a creative/destructive expression of spontaneous transformation and change, <i>could be</i> Sekhem that's basically exploded or caught fire in some spooky metaphysical way. I think if a Promethean told a (high-Memory) Mummy about the Principle, the Mummy would shrug and say that it lined up pretty well with Sutekh's Law.<br /> <br /> If I was going to include the G-M in this idea, I'd float the idea that the God-Machine's control over reality generally tamps down on the kind of uncontrolled changes that Pyros is all about, so it gets bottled up, pressurized, and explodes out of the G-Ms cold mathematical structure as Prometheans and Qashmallim. That could explain why examples of Pyros-driven phenomena are so rare but explosive when they happen; they only occur during certain localized G-M failure modes, like steam blasting through a weak weld in a pressurized vessel. EDIT: Additional thought, that could be part of why Qashmallim look like angels, because they're manifestations of Pyros coming through angel-shaped holes in the world, as it were.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to pick ypur brain about this. Was seeing similar between Sekhem and Pryos (from lots of reading i was doing on 'fallen magics') and i came up with some ideas (however poorly structured) regarding a Mummy/Demon/Promethean crossover game (ie how you would run a game where there is some similarity between these ideas...)<br /> <br /> Of course i have gone full in on the God-machine being made from the Principle (or whatever the Principle actualky looked like before it was turned into the God-machine, with the current Principle merely a shadow/ghost of what it was before...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T16:41:48-07:00","id":1523293,"title":"","content":"My favourite answer for the Principle is that it's literally a principle, a fundamental rule in creation; basically a loophole that says, in essence; &quot;fuck entropy, sometimes you really can get a free lunch&quot;. So it's not really God but you can imagine that humans reacted to occasional free lunches as gifts and miracles, and how that could give rise to legends about Prometheus and Jesus (and Sutekh).<br /> <br /> Pyros gathers in small quantities where living things plan, act on impulse, create, and destroy. That's why I think it works well as a counterpart to Sekhem: if Sekhem is generated from &quot;acts of suffering&quot;, Pyros is generated from &quot;acts of will&quot;. Although the mummies' own lore probably doesn't recognize much of a difference, since to them Sekhem obeys the laws of Suffering and Will both. That's why I characterized Pyros as Sekhem when it gets particularly energetic, since we know it does get energetic.<br /> <br /> As far as the God-Machine goes, I personally like to keep things relatively separate, so I assume the G-M is its own thing with it's own mysterious origin.<br /> It still <i>interacts</i> with the Principle, because if the principle is a universal rule of creation then everything should interact with it. And I like the idea that the G-M suppresses Pyros until it explodes out, because it seemed odd to me that if the Principle is, in fact, a universal rule, there should be a lot more evidence or manifestations of it but it's really just the Prometheans and their works and creators, and the Qashmallim.<br /> So you could imagine in a G-M-less world there could be a lot more Pyros, a lot more uncontrolled acts of will, change and destruction at a lower level of intensity, but in the CoD the GM keeps a lid on things until the lid pops off and everything catches fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T04:22:16-07:00","id":1523302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523280#post1523280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing i am not clear about is how animals reach the wellspring. Is it their representation within the Anima Mundi who seeks out the wellspring and drinks from it, and is the civilization built entirely within the Anima Mundi (or do the start forming a proto-Temenos as their souls become seperated from the Anima Mundi/World Soul? And after the civilisation collapses all that is left of the Temenos is a single realm around the Wellspring?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're correct about them being the animal representations of the Anima Mundi rather than animals themselves. I'm less convinced about them creating a new temenos, like, the text refers to it being possible to come across animal kingdoms that are still extant, and there's no mention of them being any different than any other part of the Anima Mundi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T05:05:56-07:00","id":1523303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523302#post1523302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're correct about them being the animal representations of the Anima Mundi rather than animals themselves. I'm less convinced about them creating a new temenos, like, the text refers to it being possible to come across animal kingdoms that are still extant, and there's no mention of them being any different than any other part of the Anima Mundi.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am assuming there would be other steps required... what happened with humans? Was it language and the Omphalos stones in the Astral? (And are thry related to the Hearts of Pangeans? And also what relationship do Pangeans have to the Astral?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-29T13:53:15-07:00","id":1523325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523303#post1523303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am assuming there would be other steps required... what happened with humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the difference is that it really happened. Like, we're told that the animal kingdoms fall because, ultimately, they're just dreams. Cats and bees don't actually have their own civilisations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (And are thry related to the Hearts of Pangeans? </div> </div> </div>Probably not. I gather that the omphalos stones are real artefacts recovered from the Vinca Culture. That's the name that archaeologists gave them, not the game writers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T03:33:25-07:00","id":1523344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523325#post1523325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the difference is that it really happened. Like, we're told that the animal kingdoms fall because, ultimately, they're just dreams. Cats and bees don't actually have their own civilisations.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this timeline...<br /> <br /> I feel like this dream of civilisation makes sense as a step toward how human actual civilisation came about. But it may have been one of many steps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Probably not. I gather that the omphalos stones are real artefacts recovered from the Vinca Culture. That's the name that archaeologists gave them, not the game writers. </div> </div> </div>From a tiny bit of reading, i can't find any reference to Omphalos stones rrlated to the Vinca culture, best estimate seems to he about 4,000 years later in greek and jewish traditions (which is a rough hand wavey estimate on my part, but would place them closer to today than to the Vinca).<br /> <br /> In CofD are there two things called Omphalos stones or are they the same?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T05:20:03-07:00","id":1523346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1523344#post1523344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a tiny bit of reading, i can't find any reference to Omphalos stones rrlated to the Vinca culture, best estimate seems to he about 4,000 years later in greek and jewish traditions (which is a rough hand wavey estimate on my part, but would place them closer to today than to the Vinca).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Vinca are surprisingly obscure in English (least on the internet). I had to read an archaeological dig report to find the term.<br /> <br /> But, as I said, it's a name given by <i>archaeologists</i>, ie. modern people (specifically the Serbian archaeologist Miloje Vasi\u0107). You're finding Greek references, because it's a Greek word (and object). I gather the Vinca artefacts might be termed that because they at least superficially resembled the Omphalos stone at Delphi. (Interestingly, the dig report I found mentions that Vasi\u0107 initially termed them 'jug-stoppers', presumably because they also kinda look like that.)<br /> <br /> Anyway, I dug up a comment by the developer of Mage during <i>The Sundered World</i>, Dave Brookshaw:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also also, real vinca villages had omphalos stones in them (we have taken a bit of liberty with the size, though; in reality, they were about a foot tall) - lots of cultures in the region had markers of that nature for thousands of years. Archaeologically they're called Omphaloses because, well, we have no idea what the Vinca called <i>anything</i>.\u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T03:09:57-07:00","id":1524132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1522290#post1522290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mix of bad actors, unfortunate real-estate placement, and the same basic reason the Begotten can no longer rely on the Astral to convey meaningful messages about their activities: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1356964-what-is-a-shade?p=1434797#post1434797\">there's a whole lot more people than there used to be and the overwhelming majority of them are not trained and equipped to process their trauma (nor allow their trauma to process itself)</a>, and \u2014 partially because of the aforementioned bad actors \u2014 in many cases they have been actively maladapted against doing so. Bits of the byproducts of the human soul stick around until allowed to resolve themselves, and so the inability of the disposal mechanism for those byproducts to fully break them down on its own means a horrific system of torment has been allowed to raise a rocky edifice above the drowning tides of dissolution to drag down the dead and sunder the quick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dig that alot!<br /> <br /> Geist/Mummy: To me, the Lower Depths were the place where whatever entered and stayed to long was entirely annihilated, or more accurately, devoured, because the Lower Depths <i>are </i>Ammut.<br /> <br /> Beast: The Dark Mother is much, much older than humanity, possibly even a pre-Fall entity, fear personified. No matter what timeline or world you go by, there was (un)life capable of fear, feeding the Dark Mother. In my headcanon, she is responsible or related to the creation of many splats, e.g. giving birth to Urfarah as well as having had a hand in twisting the Strix into their new shape.<br /> <br /> Mage/Demon/Promethean/Mummy/Geist:<br /> The reason the G-M seems broken and unable to progress beyond keeping a nebulous status Quo is because it literally is like a machine stuck on a process, lacking the equipment to keep going.\u200b<br /> You see, the G-M and the Principle used to be one cohesive unit with the Astral and Supernal. Originally, before the Fall, this complex natural system <i>was</i> existence: lthere was simply no real difference between the Astral, the Physical, the Spiritual, no matter what names you want to use: Duat, A'aru, Arcadia, Stygia etc. - all was one. Life before the Fall was so different, it might as well be unimaginable to us, and what we know of it, are broken faint echoes at best. There were no Watchtowers per se, but Awakening to the Principles of the Supernal was much easier due to a series of support systems, Arcana were Common, as was Knowledge about Exploits or Rites, Stepping Sideways was not limited to the Umbra not to (part-)Spirits.<br /> To achieve this unity, energies had to flow in precise orders, be transformed at correct times and dimensions through specific events, and the system that derived from this existence was carefully calibrating to ensure the different layers of realities could mesh without breaking apart or ripping parts out of each other or tearing into each other. For a 'time' for lack of a better word, this system was incredibly stable, it could even create new forms of energie and existence, enabling the system to diversify, experiment, change, transform and grow. <br /> However, at some point, balance was lost as energies fluctuated in a way the system could not compensate. As a result, everything broke, including the system. What was left separated into the world as we know it: the supernal Realms were ripped apart from everything and sorted, and the support systems conglomerated slowly into a guiding light, and finally under human guidance and influence into the Watchtowers.<br /> The rest was itself separated into many spheres: some known, some unknown, some broken and dead, some so isolated and dead they might as well not exist, most cluttering together, haphazardly teethered to each other by tenuous at best connections.<br /> <br /> The left-over pieces each continue to work in as much as they can, but are limited in functionality and input. That is why the G-M or the Principle sometimes give contradicting missions to it's agents or fail in apparently simple tasks: they are half-blind and crippled. That is why the Abyss separates the Supernal from the Fallen World, and tries to either unmake or claim the latter with seemingly little rhyme or reason. <br /> The Principle still tries to inject forms of energy to transform them into something else, the G-M still makes sure events happen, the Abyss still seperates systems from each other for transformation, and other, smaller parts certainly also still attempt to work according to how they used to... but neither can communicate with the rest anymore, their actions influencing each other in unforeseen ways, spiraling out of control, and many are, essentially, ineffectual due to an overloaded open system incapable of supporting the amount of inhabitants sustainably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-16T03:27:56-07:00","id":1524133,"title":"","content":"The 'Lower Depths are Ammut' thing is also an idea I've considered that I enjoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T09:20:54-08:00","id":1525253,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have a cool headcanon on the metaphysicial explanation of how does Carthian Law &quot;work&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27168-aeneas","name":"Aeneas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T14:18:17-08:00","id":1525269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeneas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1525253#post1525253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have a cool headcanon on the metaphysicial explanation of how does Carthian Law &quot;work&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pseudo-Old Laws of the Dead Dominions of the Underworld. Similar to the Boneyard 5 power of Sin-Eaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T14:44:37-08:00","id":1525270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeneas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1525253#post1525253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have a cool headcanon on the metaphysicial explanation of how does Carthian Law &quot;work&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>One possibility I have is that it's actually the Blood trying to tie all kindred into one clan, becoming one rather than diverging like it usually does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-11T13:25:30-08:00","id":1525358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeneas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1525253#post1525253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have a cool headcanon on the metaphysicial explanation of how does Carthian Law &quot;work&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>My headcanon is that an Astral symbol of Carth serves as an anchor to the Laws and forces them upon the souls of the living and the dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-11T13:56:45-08:00","id":1525360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeneas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1522282-favourite-answers?p=1525253#post1525253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have a cool headcanon on the metaphysicial explanation of how does Carthian Law &quot;work&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've said <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld?p=1472919#post1472919\">elsewhere</a> that the All-Night Society <i>is</i> the uniquely Kindred &quot;otherworld,&quot; and the primer in Secrets of the Covenants (plus the bit in the Hanoi story about the systems being social contract) makes as good an explainer as any for the Carthians having tapped into a ritualistically-maintained occult framework not unlike what werewolf rites tap into from the Shadow or changelings' courtly Bargains put together or how Temenotic realms tend to put their inhabitants and visitors through situations appropriate to the collectively-understood conventions of their narrative space.<br /> <br /> Just as the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1520613-what-is-the-invictus?p=1520634#post1520634\">Invictus</a> puts its focus on things that the other covenants also dip their toes into or approach from a different angle by prioritizing the conspiratorial and logistical end of the All Night Society's upkeep, the Movement's focus on adapting mortal developments to the society of the dead is to the specific end of <i>refining on what &quot;the society of the dead&quot; is</i>. That, in turn, blends with the same occult variables that are tumbling around in the whole setting (and especially the ones that concern vampires) to empower the recognized framework of rules in which social vampires operate. They're building localized versions of bans and banes and frailties into the Kindred who opt into a domain (and/or empowering existing laws to act in that capacity) by the force of the domain's recognized legitimacy and the Movement's relationship with its laws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}